====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make a [[hole]] in, especially a [[cask]] of [[liquor]], and put in a [[tap]] in order to [[draw]] the [[liquid]].
#* {{RQ:Carlyle French Revolution|text=How often has the '''broached''' barrel proved not to be for joy and heart effusion, but for duel and head-breakage.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To open, to make an opening into; to pierce.
#: {{ux|en|French knights at Agincourt were unable to '''broach''' the English line.}}
# {{senseid|en|begin discussion about}} {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To [[begin]] [[discussion]] about (something).
#: {{syn|en|spring}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''broached''' the subject of contraceptives carefully when the teenager mentioned his promiscuity.}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Sons and Lovers|passage=Yet he was much too much scared of '''broaching''' any man, let alone one in a peaked cap, to dare to ask.|4}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot||VI|text=I have tried on several occasions to '''broach''' the subject of my love to Lys; but she will not listen.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1964|month=December|title=New Books|journal=Modern Railways|page=429|text=<small>THE POCKET ENCYCLOPAEDIA OF BRITISH STEAM LOCOMOTIVES</small>. By O. S. Nock. ''Blandford Press''. 18s.<br>Mr. Nock, he remarks in his preface, was "incredulous" when the idea of this book of 192 colour gravure illustrations of a representative collection of British steam locomotives from ''Locomotion'' to BR's ''Evening Star'' was '''broached''' to him.}}
#* {{RQ:Independent|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/women-and-men-all-mouth-and-no-trousers-1575360.html|title=Women and Men: All mouth and no trousers|author=Nick Walker|date=01 October 1995|passage=Still, both [Kate] Spicer and [Anka] Radakovich think there are some subjects, even as the outrider of sexual openness, they can't '''broach'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241130091320/https://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/women-and-men-all-mouth-and-no-trousers-1575360.html|archivedate=30 November 2024}}

