===Etymology 2===
{{etystub|en}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|be turned}}{{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[turn]]ed [[sideways]] to oncoming [[wave]]s, especially large or [[break]]ing waves.
#: {{ux|en|The small boat '''broached''' and nearly sank, because of the large waves.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to turn sideways to oncoming waves, especially large or breaking waves (usually followed by ''to''; also figurative).
#* '''18th C''', {{w|Thomas Dibdin}}, ''{{w|Tom Bowling}}''
#: {{ux|en|Each time we came around into the wind, the sea '''broached''' our bow.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|ambitransitive|of a submerged [[submarine]], [[torpedo]], or similar}} To [[break]] the [[surface]] of the [[water]].
#: {{ux|en|Diving officer, '''broach''' the ship!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Tom Clancy|chapter=The Eighth Day: Friday, 10 December|title=w:The Hunt for Red October|location=Annapolis, Maryland|publisher={{w|United States Naval Institute#Naval Institute Press|Naval Institute Press}}|year=1984|page=193|isbn=0-425-13351-6|text=The ''Politovskiy'' soared through the surface of the Atlantic like a '''broaching''' whale, coming three quarters of her length out of the water before crashing back.}}

